THOUGHT: `pendingTasks.get(processingOrder.peek())` can return null if the key is absent, so `nextHolder` is nullable. I’ll add a null check to return false when it’s null, then run the prescribed Gradle command to verify that the NullAway error is resolved and no syntax errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/joos/projects/nullrepair/nullness-benchmarks/eureka && sed -i '363,365c\	      TaskHolder<ID, T> nextHolder = pendingTasks.get(processingOrder.peek());
	      if (nextHolder == null) {
	        return false;
	      }
	      long delay = System.currentTimeMillis() - nextHolder.getSubmitTimestamp();
	      return delay >= maxBatchingDelay;' eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/util/batcher/AcceptorExecutor.java && nl -ba eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/util/batcher/AcceptorExecutor.java | sed -n '355,370p' && ./gradlew eureka-core:compileJava -x test -q > build_output.log 2>&1 || grep -A 5 -B 5 'AcceptorExecutor.java' build_output.log
```

